\section*{Data availability}
The Bitcoin-OTC reputation network analyzed in this study is publicly
available~\cite{kumar2016}. The U.S.\ state-legislator follow network was
constructed from the political-elite dataset described in prior
work~\cite{biswas2025political,biswas2026attention}. Raw platform data are not
redistributed. The processed networks, the derived trust and distrust
attributes, and the preprocessing notebooks that regenerate them from the source
files are archived at Zenodo, DOI \texttt{10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX}, and are also
available at \url{https://github.com/RahaMasoumi/Gated-Network-Credence}.
Full schema and provenance documentation accompanies each dataset.

\section*{Code availability}
The custom code implementing the Gated Network Credence model, the numerical
integration and the spectral analysis, together with the scripts that reproduce
every figure reported here, is archived at Zenodo, DOI
\texttt{10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX}, and is available at
\url{https://github.com/RahaMasoumi/Gated-Network-Credence} under the MIT
license. The code is written in Python 3.10 and requires
\texttt{numpy}, \texttt{scipy}, \texttt{networkx} and \texttt{matplotlib}.
All simulations are seeded and reproduce the published panels.
